# A *fill*-engine brief: rooms by TARGET AREA (not fixed size) + adjacencies.
# The fill engine dissects the envelope so every room tiles it with no wasted
# space and habitable rooms land on the perimeter.
#
#   barndsl layout examples/oakline.brief --emit --out oakline.svg
#
# (The default engine is `fill`; `--engine greedy` runs the v1 abutment placer.)

plan "Oakline 3-Bed"
ceiling 10
note "3 bed / 2 bath, open core, bedrooms off a hall."

room living:  living   area 380
room kitchen: kitchen  area 280
room dining:  dining    area 170
room hall:    hallway  area 150 min 4
room master:  bedroom  area 224
room mbath:   bathroom area 100
room bed2:    bedroom  area 156
room bed3:    bedroom  area 156
room bath2:   bathroom area 90

adjacent living kitchen          # open core
adjacent kitchen dining
adjacent living hall             # core opens to the hall spine
adjacent hall master bed2 bed3 bath2   # bedrooms + shared bath off the hall
adjacent master mbath            # ensuite

entry living
